  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shish tawook succeeds on the marinade and the heat. The yoghurt and lemon combination does two things: it flavours the chicken and it tenderises it so that a hot grill can char the outside without drying the inside. Two hours in the fridge is the minimum; overnight is better."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The companion sauce, toum, is a pungent Lebanese garlic sauce made by emulsifying garlic, oil, and lemon. It is very strong and very good. If you have never made it, this is the right dish to start with."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use chicken thigh rather than breast. Thigh stays juicy even if slightly overcooked and takes on char much better than breast meat does."
          }
        ]
      },
